From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/qcom-mpm: complete the mailbox transfer

The APCS IPC mailbox declares neither txdone_irq nor txdone_poll, so the
core falls back to TXDONE_BY_ACK and waits for the client to tick the TX
state machine.  mpm_pd_power_off() never does: after the first
mbox_send_message() the channel's active_req stays set forever, every
later doorbell is queued behind it and never written to the IPC
register, and after MBOX_TX_QUEUE_LEN sleeps the send starts failing
with -ENOBUFS.  Only the very first sleep entry since boot ever
notified RPM.

The IPC write completes synchronously inside send_data(), so the
transfer is done the moment mbox_send_message() returns.  Acknowledge
it on the spot, like every other APCS IPC client does.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
@@ -306,6 +306,14 @@
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The APCS IPC write completes in send_data() and the channel has
+	 * no tx-done mechanism (TXDONE_BY_ACK), so tick the state machine
+	 * ourselves or the second and every later message stays queued
+	 * behind a forever-active request and never reaches RPM.
+	 */
+	mbox_client_txdone(priv->mbox_chan, 0);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
